    {
      "id": "claim_af0071d409ba41079c7282098e3359db",
      "statement": "Postgres bootstraps three distinct least-privilege roles via tools/postgres/init/10-bootstrap-roles.sh on first init: admin (superuser), migrator (non-superuser, can create schemas/tables but not roles/databases, gets MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL), and app (restricted runtime role with only schema USAGE plus DML on migrator objects, no schema CREATE, gets DATABASE_URL/CATAPULZE_DATABASE_URL). The script validates the three role names are distinct PostgreSQL identifiers, revokes PUBLIC access, and grants default privileges so the app role gets DML on future migrator-created tables.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/postgres-on-box.md#L66-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4382e80c7d44bb2750a44930cbd0aa5307da066cf63aa6ad2c5f3fdb53c573f5:"
